Vault with Ansible
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Install and configure HashiCorp Vault on a Linux system
Install and configure Ansible for automation tasks
Create Ansible playbooks to automate Vault deployment
Use Ansible to manage Vault secrets and policies
Verify automated secret retrieval and monitor Vault's operational health
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with YAML syntax
Basic knowledge of configuration management concepts
Understanding of secret management principles
Experience with text editors (nano, vim, or similar)
This lab is intended to be run on a dedicated, isolated Linux practice machine (a disposable VM or lab sandbox) that you own or control. All secrets, tokens, and credentials created in this lab are for local, educational use only and must never be reused in production systems.

Install the required tools before starting:

